                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-3487",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-3487"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2021-3487?s=debian&n=binutils&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=10&vr=%3E%3D2.31.1-16",
              "help": {
                "text": "There's a flaw in the BFD library of binutils in versions before 2.36. An attacker who supplies a crafted file to an application linked with BFD, and using the DWARF functionality, could cause an impact to system availability by way of excessive memory consumption.\n\n---\nREJECTED\n",
                "markdown": "> There's a flaw in the BFD library of binutils in versions before 2.36. An attacker who supplies a crafted file to an application linked with BFD, and using the DWARF functionality, could cause an impact to system availability by way of excessive memory consumption.\n\n---\nREJECTED\n\n|                                                                                                 |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/binutils@2.31.1-16?os_distro=buster&os_name=debian&os_version=10  |\n|Affected range  >=2.31.1-16                                                                      |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                        |\n"
